Vibration meter VM-422 is a new model produced by the VVV-Group company. A vibrometer is a vibration measurement instrument, which is designed to determine the root-mean-square speed, displacement amplitude or acceleration of vibration of mechanical components and mechanisms. Determining these parameters makes it possible to determine the quality of both new mechanical components in production and to timely assess the technical condition of mechanical components during their operation. To determine vibration parameters, VM-422 uses a high-precision piezoelectric sensor, the voltage of which is converted into device readings using an electronic microprocessor. These readings are displayed on a color graphic screen, and the vibrometer is controlled using a graphic menu and three control buttons.

Specification

Item Type: Vibration Meter VM-422 from VVV-Group
Acceleration Measurement Range 0.1-199.9m/s2(peak value)
Velocity measurement range: 0.1-199.9mm/s(real-time valid value)
Displacement Measurement Range 0.001-1.999mm(peak-peak value)
High Frequency Range: 1KHz~4KHz (HI)
Low Frequency Range: 10Hz~1KHz (LO)
Speed frequency range: 10Hz~1KHz (LO)
Displacement frequency range: 10Hz~1KHz (LO)
Maximum groupa of data storage 500 pieces (5 groups*100 pieces/group)
Power Supply: 1.5V AAA battery x2
Operating temperature: 0~40°C (32~104℉)
Humidity Range: 30~90% (non-condensing)
Dimensions: 7.1 x 2.1 x 1.2 in (180 x 54 x 30 mm)
Prode Long/Shot included in the Kit

Vibration meter VVV-Group WM-422 has the following key features:

measurement of vibration parameters: vibration velocity, vibration acceleration and displacement amplitude;
vibration frequency measurement;
selection of the frequency range when measuring vibration acceleration;
backlit color graphic display;
memory for storing measurement results;
determination of maximum, minimum, average values;
battery charge indication;
LED flashlight for taking measurements in dimly lit areas.

Operating Instructions:

MENU: Power button
MEAS: is the measurement key, press and hold this button to turn on the measurement
LO/HI: upper side
SAVE: Downside
OK: Confirm key/switch key
MEAS: bottom measurement key

Vibration Meter VM-422 can measure acceleration, rotation speed and displacement of machines and mechanisms that are widely used in mechanical production, electrical energy production, metallurgy, aircraft manufacturing, etc.

